From 8e40b59a857b1d2272f724eea2f2e088410dbf9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 09:47:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt76: mt7915: fix out-of-bounds access in SR event
 handler

Problem:
In mt7915_mcu_rx_sr_event(), when event->band_idx exceeds MT_BAND1,
the code only logs a warning but continues execution, then uses the
invalid band_idx as an array index into dev->mt76.phys[], causing an
out-of-bounds access.

Root Cause:
The invalid band_idx check only printed a message without returning.

Solution:
Return immediately after logging the invalid band idx, so an
out-of-range band_idx never reaches the array indexing path.

Feature:
Spatial Reuse

Signed-off-by: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index 85cc8266a..9464a9d06 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -561,8 +561,10 @@ mt7915_mcu_rx_sr_event(struct mt7915_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb)
 
 	event = (struct mt7915_mcu_sr_basic_event *)skb->data;
 
-	if (event->band_idx > MT_BAND1)
+	if (event->band_idx > MT_BAND1) {
 		dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "Invalid band idx %d\n", event->band_idx);
+		return;
+	}
 
 	switch (event->sub_event_id) {
 	case SPR_EVENT_CFG_SR_ENABLE:
-- 
